<h1>Simulator</h1>

<p>
  A tiny lunar lander. The main engine pushes along the craft's axis; the
  side (RCS) thrusters only rotate it, so to move sideways you tilt and burn.
  Touch down on the pad slowly, upright, and without spinning.
</p>

<div class="sim-stage">
  <canvas id="sim-canvas" width="640" height="400" aria-label="Lander simulator"></canvas>
  <p id="sim-message" class="sim-message" role="status" hidden></p>
</div>
<div class="sim-toolbar">
  <div class="sim-toggle" id="sim-pilot" role="group" aria-label="Pilot">
    <button type="button" data-value="manual" aria-pressed="true">Manual</button>
    <button type="button" data-value="pid" aria-pressed="false">PID autopilot</button>
    <button type="button" data-value="mpc" aria-pressed="false">MPC autopilot</button>
  </div>
  <div class="sim-toggle" id="sim-env" role="group" aria-label="Environment">
    <button type="button" data-value="random" aria-pressed="true">Random</button>
    <button type="button" data-value="fixed" aria-pressed="false">Reproducible</button>
  </div>
  <label class="sim-seed">Seed
    <input id="sim-seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" inputmode="numeric">
  </label>
</div>
<p class="sim-controls">
  <strong>Controls:</strong> Up / W main engine, Left / Right or A / D side
  thrusters, Space to restart. In PID mode, cascaded PID loops fly it
  instead: position to velocity to thrust and tilt, with an attitude loop on
  the side thrusters. In MPC mode, a nonlinear model predictive controller
  (generated with <a href="https://docs.acados.org/">acados</a>, compiled to
  WebAssembly) re-plans the next four seconds a hundred times a second,
  steering over the terrain under its planned path. Both fly through the same
  on/off engines as you do.
</p>
<p class="sim-controls">
  <strong>Environment:</strong> the seed sets the terrain, pad, and starting
  position and drift. Random picks a new seed each restart and shows it;
  Reproducible restarts with the seed in the box, so the same seed and the
  same pilot fly the same round. Entering a seed switches to Reproducible
  and starts it.
</p>
<p id="sim-stats" class="sim-stats"></p>
<div id="sim-plots" class="sim-plots"></div>

